    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "everyone keeps telling me to \"wait for the spark to come back\" or to \"rest,\" but they don't get it. it's not burnout. it's just... the well is dry. there's nothing left to draw from. it feels less like a struggle and more like i'm just a ghost haunting my own life, waiting for something that is never going to happen. why keep dragging this around when the story is clearly already over?",
      "source": "evaluator"
